IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cr-dates`

-- Corporations Regulations 2001 (Cth), read with the provisions of the Corporations Act 2001 they hang on: returning an
-- insurance, superannuation or investment product in the cooling-off period, and the redress a retail client can look
-- to when a licensee's service goes wrong (dispute resolution, compensation arrangements, a security bond) or a
-- broker becomes insolvent (a claim on the National Guarantee Fund).
-- Baseline encoding, from the seat of the retail client: the person who has acquired, or holds, an insurance,
-- superannuation or investment product, or receives a financial service, and wants to return the product or claim.
-- See NOTES.md for scope, the fork register and the findings.
--
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN where the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 apply: JUST FALSE where the text itself
-- says no, NOTHING where it is silent or the case falls outside its scope.
--
-- The Act's frame (ss 1019A, 1019B, 912A(1)(g), (2), 912B) is quoted from the Corporations Act 2001 as deposited at
-- ../../../corporations-act-2001/registers/source-bundle/C2004A00818.txt; the Regulations cannot be read without it.

§ `Cooling-off, complaints and compensation: what the retail client can do`

§§ `Act s 1019A, reg 7.9.64 -- do I have a cooling-off right for my product`

-- Act s 1019A(1)(a): the Division applies if a product of one of these classes is provided to a person "as a retail
-- client": (i) risk insurance products (general insurance and life risk insurance, s 764A(1)(d), (e)); (ii) investment
-- life insurance products; (iii) managed investment products; (iiia) foreign passport fund products; (iv)
-- superannuation products; (v) RSAs (retirement savings accounts). A security in a CCIV is not in the deposited list,
-- though reg 7.9.64(1)(ea), (hb) assume the Division can reach one (fork: NOTHING).
DECLARE `A kind of financial product` IS ONE OF
    `a risk insurance product`
    `an investment life insurance product`
    `a managed investment product`
    `a foreign passport fund product`
    `a superannuation product`
    `an RSA`
    `a security in a CCIV`
    `another kind of financial product`

-- reg 7.9.64(1): the subclasses "excluded from paragraph 1019A(1)(a)". Paragraph (g) (short renewals of risk insurance)
-- is worked out from two facts instead of being chosen here.
--   (a) distribution reinvestment plan or switching facility; (b) additional contribution under an existing agreement;
--   (c) consideration under a takeover bid; (d) interim contract of insurance (ICA s 11(2)); (e), (ea) a scheme or CCIV
--   sub-fund not liquid at issue; (f) super from a fund that is not a public offer fund (other than a product taken to
--   be issued under reg 7.1.04E or an annuity or pension under reg 7.9.02(4)); (fa) super from a public offer fund in
--   reg 7.6.01(1)(b)-(d) (pooled superannuation trusts), a successor fund, or an eligible rollover fund under SIS Act
--   Part 24 or RSA Act Part 9; (fb) a pension from a fund whose rules allow benefits only as a pension from that fund;
--   (h), (ha), (hb) a product to which s 1016D(1) applies (its disclosure statement said it would be tradeable on a
--   market); (i) a scheme interest under the old Chapter 6D that was listed before the FSR commencement.
DECLARE `How I came to hold the product` IS ONE OF
    `in none of the excluded ways`
    `under a distribution reinvestment plan or switching facility`
    `as an additional contribution under an existing agreement or contract`
    `as consideration under a takeover bid`
    `under an interim contract of insurance`
    `as an interest in a scheme or CCIV sub-fund that was not liquid when issued`
    `as a super product of a fund that is not a public offer fund`
    `as a super product of a pooled trust, successor fund or eligible rollover fund`
    `as a pension from a fund whose rules allow benefits only as a pension`
    `as a product its disclosure statement said would be tradeable on a market`
    `as a scheme interest listed under the old Chapter 6D before the FSR commencement`

GIVEN `the way` IS A `How I came to hold the product`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the way is an excluded subclass` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `in none of the excluded ways` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- reg 7.9.64(1)(g): "a risk insurance product that is: (i) of less than 12 months duration; and (ii) a renewal of an
-- existing product on the terms and conditions to which the product is currently subject".
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product`
      `the cover runs for less than 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it renews existing cover on its current terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is an excluded short renewal of risk insurance` MEANS
        `the kind` EQUALS `a risk insurance product`
    AND `the cover runs for less than 12 months`
    AND `it renews existing cover on its current terms`

@export Do I have a cooling-off right to return this insurance, super or investment product and get my money back (Corporations Act s 1019A; Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.64)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product: a risk insurance product (general insurance such as car, home or travel cover, or life risk cover such as life, TPD, trauma or income protection), an investment life insurance product, a managed investment product, a foreign passport fund product, a superannuation product, an RSA, a security in a CCIV, or another kind of financial product
      `I acquired it as a retail client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the product provided to you as a retail client (an ordinary consumer, not a wholesale or professional investor)?
      `it was issued to me or sold to me under an offer needing a disclosure statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the product issued to you, or sold to you under an offer to which s 1012C applies (a sale offer that needs a Product Disclosure Statement)? Answer no for an ordinary purchase from another holder.
      `the way` IS A `How I came to hold the product` @desc Did you get it in one of the excluded ways (a distribution reinvestment plan or switch, an additional contribution under an existing agreement, a takeover bid, an interim contract of insurance, an illiquid scheme, a non-public-offer super fund, a pooled, successor or eligible rollover fund, a pension-only fund, a product promised to be tradeable on a market, an old listed scheme interest)? Otherwise choose none.
      `the cover runs for less than 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For insurance: does the cover run for less than 12 months?
      `it renews existing cover on its current terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For insurance: is it a renewal of cover you already had, on the terms it is currently subject to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a cooling-off right for my product` IS
    IF `the kind` EQUALS `a security in a CCIV`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `the kind` EQUALS `another kind of financial product`
             OR (NOT `I acquired it as a retail client`)
             OR (NOT `it was issued to me or sold to me under an offer needing a disclosure statement`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF     `the way is an excluded subclass` `the way`
                  OR `it is an excluded short renewal of risk insurance` `the kind` `the cover runs for less than 12 months` `it renews existing cover on its current terms`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Act s 1019B(2), reg 7.9.64A -- how I must tell the issuer I am returning it`

DECLARE `A way of notifying` IS ONE OF
    `in writing`
    `electronically`
    `another way, such as by phone`

-- Act s 1019B(2): "The right to return the product must be exercised by notifying the responsible person in one of the
-- following ways: (a) in writing; or (b) electronically; or (c) in any other way specified in the regulations."
-- reg 7.9.64A: for a risk insurance product, also "by notifying the responsible person in a way permitted by the
-- responsible person". The list is closed ("one of the following ways"), so any other way is a no.
@export Is this a way I may give notice that I am returning my product in the cooling-off period (Corporations Act s 1019B(2); Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.64A)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (risk insurance, investment life insurance, managed investment, foreign passport fund, superannuation, RSA, CCIV security, or another kind)
      `the way` IS A `A way of notifying` @desc How you notify the issuer or seller: in writing, electronically (e.g. email or an online form), or another way such as by phone
      `the issuer permits that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer or seller permit notice to be given that way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a way I may notify my return` IS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `electronically` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST (`the kind` EQUALS `a risk insurance product` AND `the issuer permits that way`)

§§ `Act s 1019B(3), (4) -- when my 14-day cooling-off period starts and ends`

-- Act s 1019B(3): the right "can only be exercised during the period of 14 days starting on the earlier of: (a) the
-- time when the confirmation requirement (if applicable) is complied with; or (b) the end of the fifth business day
-- after the day on which the product was issued or sold to the client". (4): the confirmation requirement is complied
-- with when the client receives confirmation of the transaction (or it is available through a facility).
-- Read here: a period starting at a time on day D runs to the end of day D + 14 (the starting day is not counted as one
-- of the 14); a period starting at the end of day D runs from D + 1 to D + 14. The first day on which the right may be
-- used is the confirmation day, or the day after the fifth business day. See the fork register.
GIVEN `the day it was issued or sold to me` IS A DATE
      `I received confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received confirmation` IS A DATE
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the period starts at confirmation` MEANS
        `I received confirmation`
    AND `is on or before` `the day I received confirmation` (`the Nth business day after` `the day it was issued or sold to me` 5 `holidays`)

GIVEN `the day it was issued or sold to me` IS A DATE
      `I received confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received confirmation` IS A DATE
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the cooling-off period` MEANS
    IF `the period starts at confirmation` `the day it was issued or sold to me` `I received confirmation` `the day I received confirmation` `holidays`
    THEN `the day I received confirmation`
    ELSE `the day N days after` (`the Nth business day after` `the day it was issued or sold to me` 5 `holidays`) 1

@export What is the last day of my 14-day cooling-off period, before any extension for a last day that is a weekend or holiday (Corporations Act s 1019B(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day it was issued or sold to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the product was issued or sold to you (ISO date)
      `I received confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received confirmation of the transaction (or is it available to you through an online facility)?
      `the day I received confirmation` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the confirmation, or it became available to you (ISO date; any date if you have not)
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The public holidays and bank holidays in your place in the three weeks after the product was issued (ISO dates; may be empty)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `The last day of my cooling-off period` IS
    IF `the period starts at confirmation` `the day it was issued or sold to me` `I received confirmation` `the day I received confirmation` `holidays`
    THEN `the day N days after` `the day I received confirmation` 14
    ELSE `the day N days after` (`the Nth business day after` `the day it was issued or sold to me` 5 `holidays`) 14

§§ `Act s 1019B(3), (5), regs 7.9.65(1), 7.9.70 -- can I still return it on this day`

-- Act s 1019B(5): the right "cannot be exercised at any time after: (a) the client has ... exercised a right or power
-- that they have under the terms applicable to the product" (for insurance, making a claim); "or (b) the time ... at
-- which, under the terms applicable to the product, the client's rights or powers in respect of the product end".
-- reg 7.9.70(2): receiving a distribution is not exercising a right or power.
-- reg 7.9.65(1): for a risk insurance product "for an event that will start and end within the 14 day period" (e.g.
-- short-term travel insurance; the event is the start of the journey, or of loading for a removal), the right cannot be
-- exercised after the earlier of the end of the 14-day period and "the start of the event".
@export If I have a cooling-off right, can I still return my product on this day (Corporations Act s 1019B(3), (5); Corporations Regulations regs 7.9.65(1), 7.9.70)?
GIVEN `the day it was issued or sold to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the product was issued or sold to you (ISO date)
      `I received confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received confirmation of the transaction (or is it available to you through an online facility)?
      `the day I received confirmation` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the confirmation (ISO date; any date if you have not)
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The public holidays and bank holidays in your place in the three weeks after the product was issued (ISO dates; may be empty)
      `the day I notify` IS A DATE @desc The day you notify the issuer or seller that you are returning the product (ISO date)
      `I have made a claim or used another right under the product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before notifying, had you made a claim or used any other right or power under the product's terms? Receiving a distribution does not count.
      `my rights under the product end on a set day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the product's terms, do your rights end on a set day (e.g. one-week cover)?
      `the day my rights end` IS A DATE @desc The day your rights under the product end (ISO date; any date if they do not)
      `it insures an event that starts and ends within the 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it risk insurance for an event (e.g. a trip, or a removal) that starts and ends within the 14-day cooling-off period?
      `the event had started when I notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, had the event (e.g. the journey) started when you notified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still return my product on this day` IS
    IF     `is before` `the day I notify` (`the first day of the cooling-off period` `the day it was issued or sold to me` `I received confirmation` `the day I received confirmation` `holidays`)
        OR `is before` (`The last day of my cooling-off period` `the day it was issued or sold to me` `I received confirmation` `the day I received confirmation` `holidays`) `the day I notify`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     `I have made a claim or used another right under the product`
             OR (`my rights under the product end on a set day` AND `is before` `the day my rights end` `the day I notify`)
             OR (`it insures an event that starts and ends within the 14 days` AND `the event had started when I notified`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `reg 7.9.65(1A) -- scheme interests acquired together`

-- reg 7.9.65(1A): if a person acquires an interest in a managed investment scheme that is a managed investment product
-- or foreign passport fund product, and "acquires one or more other interests in that managed investment scheme in the
-- course of the same transaction", "the person cannot exercise a right to return the product otherwise than by returning
-- all of those interests".
@export Must I return all the scheme interests I acquired in the same transaction, rather than only some (Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.65(1A))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (a managed investment product or foreign passport fund product is what this rule covers)
      `I acquired other interests in the same scheme in the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire one or more other interests in the same scheme in the same transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I return all my scheme interests together` IS
    IF     (`the kind` EQUALS `a managed investment product` OR `the kind` EQUALS `a foreign passport fund product`)
       AND `I acquired other interests in the same scheme in the same transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `reg 7.9.66 -- returning super or an RSA: nominating a fund for preserved money`

-- reg 7.9.66(2): for a superannuation product or RSA, if the money to be repaid includes restricted non-preserved or
-- preserved benefits (SIS Regulations terms: money that cannot yet be paid out in cash), "the holder of the product must
-- nominate a superannuation entity or RSA into which" that money "is to be repaid". (3): "The right of return is taken to
-- have been exercised only on receipt by the responsible person of the nomination." (4): "The holder must make the
-- nomination not later than 1 month after notifying the responsible person". (5): in writing or by electronic means.
-- (7): "the responsible person must return the money as directed".

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is super or an RSA` MEANS
    `the kind` EQUALS `a superannuation product` OR `the kind` EQUALS `an RSA`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product`
      `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a nomination is required` MEANS
        `it is super or an RSA` `the kind`
    AND `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits`

@export To return my super or RSA in the cooling-off period, must I nominate another fund or RSA for the money (Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.66(2))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (a superannuation product or an RSA is what this rule covers)
      `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money to be repaid include preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits (super you cannot yet take in cash)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I nominate a fund to return my super` IS
    IF (NOT (`it is super or an RSA` `the kind`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`a nomination is required` `the kind` `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits`)

-- The last day for the nomination: "not later than 1 month after notifying", read as the same day of the next month
-- (a day the next month lacks becomes its last day).
GIVEN `the day I notified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to nominate` MEANS
    `the day N months after` `the day I notified` 1

@export By when must I nominate a fund or RSA for my preserved super, after notifying that I am returning my super or RSA (Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.66(4))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (a superannuation product or an RSA is what this rule covers)
      `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money to be repaid include preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits?
      `the day I notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you notified the fund or RSA provider that you are returning the product (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must I nominate a fund for my super` IS
    IF `a nomination is required` `the kind` `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits`
    THEN JUST (`the last day to nominate` `the day I notified`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The nomination duty as a regulative rule, counted in days from the notification. The responsible person's duty to
-- return the money as directed (reg 7.9.66(7)) follows it, with no time stated in the text.
DECLARE `A party to my return` IS ONE OF `the holder`, `the responsible person`
DECLARE `A step in my return` IS ONE OF
    `nominate a superannuation entity or RSA`
    `return the money as directed`

GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to my return` `A step in my return`
`the nomination duty` MEANS
    PARTY `the holder`
    MUST `nominate a superannuation entity or RSA`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the holder` BECAUSE "no nomination within 1 month after notifying: the return is not taken to be exercised (reg 7.9.66(3), (4))"

GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to my return` `A step in my return`
`the return of my super` MEANS
    PARTY `the holder`
    MUST `nominate a superannuation entity or RSA`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the responsible person`
        MUST `return the money as directed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the holder` BECAUSE "no nomination within 1 month after notifying: the return is not taken to be exercised (reg 7.9.66(3), (4))"

GIVEN `the day I notified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days allowed to nominate` MEANS
    `the day number of` (`the last day to nominate` `the day I notified`) MINUS `the day number of` `the day I notified`

GIVEN `the day I notified` IS A DATE
      `the day my nomination was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the nomination came in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the nomination duty` (`days allowed to nominate` `the day I notified`)) (`the day number of` `the day I notified`) (LIST (EVENT `the holder` `nominate a superannuation entity or RSA` (`the day number of` `the day my nomination was received`)))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Has my return of my super or RSA in the cooling-off period taken effect by this day (Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.66(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (a superannuation product or an RSA is what this rule covers)
      `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money to be repaid include preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits?
      `the day I notified` IS A DATE @desc The day you notified that you are returning the product (ISO date)
      `I have nominated a fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the fund or RSA provider received your nomination of another fund or RSA for the money?
      `the day my nomination was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the nomination was received (ISO date; any date if not)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my return of my super taken effect` IS
    IF (NOT (`it is super or an RSA` `the kind`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `the money includes preserved or restricted non-preserved benefits`)
         THEN JUST (`is on or before` `the day I notified` `the day asked about`)
         ELSE JUST (    `I have nominated a fund`
                    AND `is on or before` `the day my nomination was received` `the day asked about`
                    AND `is on or before` `the day I notified` `the day my nomination was received`
                    AND `the nomination came in time` `the day I notified` `the day my nomination was received`)

-- reg 7.9.66(6): "if: (a) a holder nominates a superannuation entity or RSA; and (b) the superannuation entity or RSA
-- does not accept the nomination; the responsible person may rollover or transfer the holder's benefits to an eligible
-- rollover fund."
@export If the fund I nominated will not accept my super, may it be moved to an eligible rollover fund instead (Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.66(6))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (a superannuation product or an RSA is what this rule covers)
      `I nominated a fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you nominate a super fund or RSA for the money?
      `the nominated fund does not accept it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the fund or RSA you nominated refused to accept the nomination?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my super go to an eligible rollover fund` IS
    IF (NOT (`it is super or an RSA` `the kind`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`I nominated a fund` AND `the nominated fund does not accept it`)

§§ `Act s 1019B(1), (8), reg 7.9.67 -- how much I get back`

-- Act s 1019B(1): the client may "have the money they paid to acquire the product repaid"; (8): the regulations may
-- increase or reduce it. reg 7.9.67:
-- (2), (3): for an investment-linked life product (ICA meaning), a managed investment product, a foreign passport fund
--   product, a CCIV security or a superannuation product, if the price on the day the issuer receives the notice is
--   lower than the price at acquisition the amount "may be reduced by the adjustment amount"; if higher, it "is
--   increased by the adjustment amount". (4): the adjustment amount is the difference between the two prices.
-- (6): unrecoverable tax or duty paid or payable by the issuer because of the issue: the amount "is reduced".
-- (7): for any product other than an RSA, it "may be reduced to account for reasonable administrative and transaction
--   costs (other than ... commissions ...)" that are reasonably related to the acquisition and termination and do not
--   exceed the true cost of an arm's length transaction.
-- (8): risk insurance issued, or paid for, for a specific period: "may be reduced by a proportion equal to the
--   proportion of the period that has passed". Read here as a proportion of the premium for that period (the risk
--   insurance part of the product); see the fork register.
-- (9): a distribution to which reg 7.9.70(2) applies: "may be reduced by the amount of that distribution".
-- "may" reductions are the issuer's choice; "is" changes are not. The answer is therefore a range: the least I can be
-- repaid (every permitted reduction taken) and the most (only the changes the text requires). Neither goes below zero.

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product`
      `it is investment-linked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the price adjustment applies` MEANS
       (`the kind` EQUALS `an investment life insurance product` AND `it is investment-linked`)
    OR `the kind` EQUALS `a managed investment product`
    OR `the kind` EQUALS `a foreign passport fund product`
    OR `the kind` EQUALS `a security in a CCIV`
    OR `the kind` EQUALS `a superannuation product`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` MEANS
    IF `x` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `x`

DECLARE `The facts of my repayment` HAS
    `product kind` IS A `A kind of financial product`
    `investment-linked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `money paid` IS A NUMBER
    `price at acquisition` IS A NUMBER
    `price on the notice day` IS A NUMBER
    `tax or duty not recoverable` IS A NUMBER
    `administrative and transaction costs` IS A NUMBER
    `premium for a specific period` IS A NUMBER
    `days in the period` IS A NUMBER
    `days passed` IS A NUMBER
    `distributions` IS A NUMBER

-- The amount after the changes the text requires: (3) a rise in price is added, (6) unrecoverable tax or duty is taken
-- off.
GIVEN `f` IS A `The facts of my repayment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the required amount` MEANS
    (`f`'s `money paid` PLUS `the rise`) MINUS `f`'s `tax or duty not recoverable`
    WHERE
        `the rise` MEANS
            IF     `the price adjustment applies` (`f`'s `product kind`) (`f`'s `investment-linked`)
               AND `f`'s `price on the notice day` GREATER THAN `f`'s `price at acquisition`
            THEN `f`'s `price on the notice day` MINUS `f`'s `price at acquisition`
            ELSE 0

-- The reductions the issuer may choose to take: (2) a fall in price, (7) costs (not for an RSA), (8) the passed
-- proportion of a specific-period premium, (9) distributions (for the products in reg 7.9.70(1)).
GIVEN `f` IS A `The facts of my repayment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the permitted reductions` MEANS
    `the fall` PLUS `the cost reduction` PLUS `the period reduction` PLUS `the distribution reduction`
    WHERE
        `adjustment applies` MEANS `the price adjustment applies` (`f`'s `product kind`) (`f`'s `investment-linked`)
        `the fall` MEANS
            IF `adjustment applies` AND `f`'s `price on the notice day` LESS THAN `f`'s `price at acquisition`
            THEN `f`'s `price at acquisition` MINUS `f`'s `price on the notice day`
            ELSE 0
        `the cost reduction` MEANS
            IF `f`'s `product kind` EQUALS `an RSA` THEN 0 ELSE `f`'s `administrative and transaction costs`
        `the period reduction` MEANS
            IF `f`'s `days in the period` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN (`f`'s `premium for a specific period` TIMES `f`'s `days passed`) DIVIDED BY `f`'s `days in the period`
            ELSE 0
        `the distribution reduction` MEANS
            IF `adjustment applies` THEN `f`'s `distributions` ELSE 0

@export If I return my product in the cooling-off period, what is the least the issuer can repay me, taking every reduction the Regulations allow (Corporations Act s 1019B(1), (8); Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.67)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (risk insurance, investment life insurance, managed investment, foreign passport fund, superannuation, RSA, CCIV security, or another kind)
      `it is investment-linked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For investment life insurance: is it an investment-linked product (its value follows units in an investment fund)?
      `the money I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The money you paid to acquire the product, in dollars
      `the price when I acquired it` IS A NUMBER @desc For a unit-priced product: what the product cost at the price on the day you acquired it, in dollars (use the money you paid if it has no unit price)
      `the price on the day my notice was received` IS A NUMBER @desc For a unit-priced product: what the same product would cost at the price on the day the issuer received your notice, in dollars (or at the most recent price before that)
      `unrecoverable tax or duty` IS A NUMBER @desc Tax or duty the issuer paid or must pay because of issuing the product and cannot get back, in dollars (0 if none)
      `reasonable administrative and transaction costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The issuer's reasonable administrative and transaction costs of the acquisition and termination, not counting commissions and not above an arm's length cost, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the premium for cover for a specific period` IS A NUMBER @desc For insurance cover issued or paid for a specific period: the premium for that period, in dollars (0 if none)
      `days in that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days that period of cover runs (0 if none)
      `days of it already passed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of that period had passed when you returned the product
      `distributions I received` IS A NUMBER @desc Distributions you received on the product before returning it, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The least I can be repaid` IS
    `not below zero` (`the required amount` `the facts` MINUS `the permitted reductions` `the facts`)
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `The facts of my repayment` WITH
            `product kind` IS `the kind`
            `investment-linked` IS `it is investment-linked`
            `money paid` IS `the money I paid`
            `price at acquisition` IS `the price when I acquired it`
            `price on the notice day` IS `the price on the day my notice was received`
            `tax or duty not recoverable` IS `unrecoverable tax or duty`
            `administrative and transaction costs` IS `reasonable administrative and transaction costs`
            `premium for a specific period` IS `the premium for cover for a specific period`
            `days in the period` IS `days in that period`
            `days passed` IS `days of it already passed`
            `distributions` IS `distributions I received`

@export If I return my product in the cooling-off period, what is the most I can be repaid, if the issuer takes none of the reductions it may choose (Corporations Act s 1019B(1), (8); Corporations Regulations reg 7.9.67)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `A kind of financial product` @desc The kind of product (risk insurance, investment life insurance, managed investment, foreign passport fund, superannuation, RSA, CCIV security, or another kind)
      `it is investment-linked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For investment life insurance: is it an investment-linked product (its value follows units in an investment fund)?
      `the money I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The money you paid to acquire the product, in dollars
      `the price when I acquired it` IS A NUMBER @desc For a unit-priced product: what the product cost at the price on the day you acquired it, in dollars (use the money you paid if it has no unit price)
      `the price on the day my notice was received` IS A NUMBER @desc For a unit-priced product: what the same product would cost at the price on the day the issuer received your notice, in dollars (or at the most recent price before that)
      `unrecoverable tax or duty` IS A NUMBER @desc Tax or duty the issuer paid or must pay because of issuing the product and cannot get back, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The most I can be repaid` IS
    `not below zero` (`the required amount` `the facts`)
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `The facts of my repayment` WITH
            `product kind` IS `the kind`
            `investment-linked` IS `it is investment-linked`
            `money paid` IS `the money I paid`
            `price at acquisition` IS `the price when I acquired it`
            `price on the notice day` IS `the price on the day my notice was received`
            `tax or duty not recoverable` IS `unrecoverable tax or duty`
            `administrative and transaction costs` IS 0
            `premium for a specific period` IS 0
            `days in the period` IS 0
            `days passed` IS 0
            `distributions` IS 0

§§ `Act s 912A(1)(g), (2), reg 7.6.02(5), (6) -- must my licensee have a complaints system and belong to AFCA`

-- Act s 912A(1)(g): a licensee must, "if those financial services are provided to persons as retail clients", have a
-- dispute resolution system complying with (2): (a) an internal dispute resolution procedure, and (c) "membership of the
-- AFCA scheme" (the Australian Financial Complaints Authority).
-- reg 7.6.02(5): a licensee providing a service as (a) a trustee under a will or on intestacy, (b) a trustee of an
-- express trust whose settlor is a natural person and whose interest is not a financial product, or (c) an attorney
-- under an enduring power of attorney "does not have to comply with paragraph 912A(2)(c)" (AFCA membership) "if
-- complaints about the service ... may be made to the Ombudsman of a State or Territory".
-- reg 7.6.02(6): a licensee providing a service "as administrator of the estate of an individual" "does not have to
-- comply with paragraph 912A(1)(g)" (the whole system) if complaints "may be made under a State or Territory law listed
-- in Schedule 8AC" (the guardianship and trustee laws of each State and Territory, 15 items).
DECLARE `The capacity my licensee acts in` IS ONE OF
    `as a trustee under a will or on an intestacy`
    `as a trustee of an express trust`
    `as an attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
    `as the administrator of an individual's estate`
    `in another capacity, such as adviser, insurer, super fund or product issuer`

DECLARE `The complaints system my licensee must have` IS ONE OF
    `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
    `an internal procedure, but AFCA membership is not required`
    `no dispute resolution system is required by s 912A(1)(g)`

@export For my complaint, must the licensee have an internal complaints procedure and belong to AFCA (Corporations Act s 912A(1)(g), (2); Corporations Regulations reg 7.6.02(5), (6))?
GIVEN `I am a retail client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the financial service provided to you (or the person you act for) as a retail client?
      `the capacity` IS A `The capacity my licensee acts in` @desc The capacity the licensee provides the service in: trustee under a will or intestacy, trustee of an express trust, attorney under an enduring power of attorney, administrator of an individual's estate (e.g. a financial manager appointed under guardianship law), or another capacity
      `the settlor was a natural person and the trust interest is not a financial product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an express trust: was the trust set up by an individual, and is the interest in it not a financial product?
      `complaints may be made to a State or Territory Ombudsman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can complaints about the service be made to the Ombudsman of a State or Territory?
      `complaints may be made under a Schedule 8AC law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an estate administrator: can complaints about the service be made under a State or Territory guardianship or trustee law listed in Schedule 8AC of the Regulations?
GIVETH A `The complaints system my licensee must have`
DECIDE `What complaints system must my licensee have` IS
    IF (NOT `I am a retail client`)
    THEN `no dispute resolution system is required by s 912A(1)(g)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the capacity`
         WHEN `as the administrator of an individual's estate` THEN
            IF `complaints may be made under a Schedule 8AC law`
            THEN `no dispute resolution system is required by s 912A(1)(g)`
            ELSE `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
         WHEN `as a trustee under a will or on an intestacy` THEN `relieved of AFCA if an Ombudsman`
         WHEN `as an attorney under an enduring power of attorney` THEN `relieved of AFCA if an Ombudsman`
         WHEN `as a trustee of an express trust` THEN
            IF `the settlor was a natural person and the trust interest is not a financial product`
            THEN `relieved of AFCA if an Ombudsman`
            ELSE `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
         OTHERWISE `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`
    WHERE
        `relieved of AFCA if an Ombudsman` MEANS
            IF `complaints may be made to a State or Territory Ombudsman`
            THEN `an internal procedure, but AFCA membership is not required`
            ELSE `an internal procedure and AFCA membership`

§§ `Act s 912B, reg 7.6.02AAA -- must my licensee hold professional indemnity insurance to compensate me`

-- Act s 912B(1): a licensee providing a financial service to persons as retail clients "must have arrangements for
-- compensating those persons for loss or damage suffered because of breaches of the relevant obligations"; (2) the
-- arrangements must satisfy the regulations or be approved in writing by ASIC.
-- reg 7.6.02AAA(1): the arrangements are, "unless the financial services licensee is an exempt licensee, subject to the
-- requirement that the licensee hold professional indemnity insurance cover that is adequate" (having regard to AFCA
-- membership, the realistic maximum liability, and the size and kind of business). Adequacy is not decided here.
-- (3): exempt licensee "means" (a) an APRA-regulated general insurer, life insurer or authorised deposit-taking
-- institution (ADI, e.g. a bank), or (b) a related licensee for which such a body has given a guarantee, adequate under
-- (1), "approved in writing by ASIC".
DECLARE `The kind of licensee` IS ONE OF
    `an APRA-regulated general insurer`
    `an APRA-regulated life insurer`
    `an APRA-regulated bank or other ADI`
    `a licensee related to an insurer or ADI`
    `another licensee, such as an advice business`

@export Must the licensee that serves me as a retail client hold professional indemnity insurance as part of its arrangements to compensate me (Corporations Act s 912B; Corporations Regulations reg 7.6.02AAA)?
GIVEN `I am a retail client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the financial service provided to you as a retail client?
      `the licensee` IS A `The kind of licensee` @desc What kind of licensee it is: an APRA-regulated general insurer, life insurer or bank (ADI), a licensee related to one of those, or another licensee such as an advice business
      `ASIC approved a guarantee from the related insurer or ADI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a related licensee: has ASIC approved in writing a guarantee from the insurer or ADI that ensures payment of the licensee's obligations to its retail clients?
      `ASIC approved other compensation arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has ASIC approved in writing the licensee's compensation arrangements under s 912B(2)(b), instead of the regulations' requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my licensee hold PI insurance to compensate me` IS
    IF (NOT `I am a retail client`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the licensee is exempt`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `ASIC approved other compensation arrangements`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the licensee is exempt` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the licensee`
            WHEN `an APRA-regulated general insurer` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an APRA-regulated life insurer` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an APRA-regulated bank or other ADI` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a licensee related to an insurer or ADI` THEN `ASIC approved a guarantee from the related insurer or ADI`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `reg 7.6.02AA(4), (5) -- claiming against a licensee's security bond held by ASIC`

-- reg 7.6.02AA(4): a security bond lodged with ASIC "may be released by ASIC, at its discretion, if" (a) ASIC considers
-- it is no longer required (the licensee now complies with s 912B(1) or is exempt); (b) ASIC has published a proposal to
-- release it and a web address; (c) ASIC has advertised the bond there, "and an invitation to submit valid claims
-- against the bond"; and (d) "3 months after publication of the advertisement, no valid claim has been submitted".
-- Read here: a valid claim submitted on or before the day 3 months after the advertisement blocks release under (4).
-- This is a situation only some clients meet: a licensee that once lodged a bond in place of compensation arrangements.

GIVEN `the day the advertisement was published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a claim against the bond` MEANS
    `the day N months after` `the day the advertisement was published` 3

@export By when must I submit my claim against a licensee's security bond, after ASIC advertises that it proposes to release it (Corporations Regulations reg 7.6.02AA(4)(c), (d))?
GIVEN `the day the advertisement was published` IS A DATE @desc The day ASIC published the advertisement inviting claims against the bond (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I claim against the security bond` IS
    `the last day for a claim against the bond` `the day the advertisement was published`

@export On this day, may ASIC release a licensee's security bond against which I could claim (Corporations Regulations reg 7.6.02AA(4))?
GIVEN `ASIC considers the bond no longer required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does ASIC consider the bond no longer required, because the licensee now has compliant compensation arrangements or is an exempt licensee?
      `ASIC published the proposal and advertised the bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has ASIC published, accessibly and reasonably prominently, a proposal to release the bond with a web address, and advertised the bond there with an invitation to claim?
      `the day the advertisement was published` IS A DATE @desc The day the advertisement was published (ISO date)
      `I submitted a valid claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you submitted a valid claim against the bond?
      `the day I submitted my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you submitted it (ISO date; any date if you have not)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May ASIC release the security bond` IS
    IF     `ASIC considers the bond no longer required`
       AND `ASIC published the proposal and advertised the bond`
       AND `is before` (`the last day for a claim against the bond` `the day the advertisement was published`) `the day asked about`
       AND (NOT (`I submitted a valid claim` AND `is on or before` `the day I submitted my claim` (`the last day for a claim against the bond` `the day the advertisement was published`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 7.5 Subdivision 4.9, regs 7.5.64, 7.5.67-7.5.69 -- claiming on the National Guarantee Fund when my broker becomes insolvent`

-- This group arises only if a market participant (a broker) who held money or securities for me has become insolvent.
-- reg 7.5.64(1): "A person may make a claim in respect of property if: (a) a dealer has become insolvent ...; and (b) at
-- an earlier time ... the property was, in the course of, or in connection with, the dealer's securities business
-- entrusted to, or received by" the dealer (or its participant firm, partner or employee) "on behalf of, or because the
-- dealer was a trustee of the property for, the person (other than an excluded person in relation to the dealer); and
-- (c) at the time the dealer became insolvent, the obligations of the dealer ... to the person in respect of the
-- property have not been discharged."
-- reg 7.5.04: an excluded person is, in short, the participant itself and people and companies close to it (its
-- officers, partners, their spouses and relatives, trusts they can benefit from, companies they control). Asked as a fact.
-- reg 7.5.67: no claim for money lent to the dealer. reg 7.5.68: no claim unless, at the insolvency, the dealer was a
-- participant of a participating market licensee (a member of the SEGC) or of the CS facility operated by ACH, and was
-- carrying on (or last carried on) a securities business in Australia. reg 7.5.69: no claim if (a) the property had
-- already ceased, in due course of administering a trust, to be under the dealer's sole control, or (b) the SEGC or the
-- Court is satisfied that the claimant's act or omission materially contributed to the insolvency (asked as a fact).
@export Can I claim on the National Guarantee Fund for money or securities my insolvent broker held for me (Corporations Regulations regs 7.5.64(1), 7.5.67, 7.5.68, 7.5.69)?
GIVEN `the broker has become insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the broker (the market participant) become insolvent?
      `the property was entrusted to or received by the broker for me in its securities business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the money or property entrusted to, or received by, the broker (or its firm, partner or employee) on your behalf or on trust for you, in connection with its securities business?
      `its obligations to me for the property were undischarged at the insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the broker became insolvent, had it still not met its obligations to you for that property?
      `I am an excluded person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an excluded person: the broker itself, or (in short) one of its officers or partners, their spouse or relative, a trust they can benefit from, or a company they control?
      `the property is money I lent to the broker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim for money you lent to the broker?
      `the broker was a participant of an SEGC-member market or ACH's clearing facility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the insolvency, was the broker a participant of a market whose operator is a member of the SEGC (e.g. ASX), or of the clearing facility operated by ACH?
      `the broker carried on its securities business in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the insolvency, was the broker carrying on a securities business in Australia (or was that its last business in Australia, and your claim relates to it)?
      `the property had left the broker's sole control in administering a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the insolvency, had the property ceased to be under the broker's sole control in the ordinary course of administering a trust?
      `the SEGC or Court is satisfied I contributed to the insolvency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the SEGC or the Court satisfied that something you did or failed to do materially contributed to the broker becoming insolvent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim on the NGF for property my insolvent broker held` IS
    IF     `the broker has become insolvent`
       AND `the property was entrusted to or received by the broker for me in its securities business`
       AND `its obligations to me for the property were undischarged at the insolvency`
       AND (NOT `I am an excluded person`)
       AND (NOT `the property is money I lent to the broker`)
       AND `the broker was a participant of an SEGC-member market or ACH's clearing facility`
       AND `the broker carried on its securities business in Australia`
       AND (NOT `the property had left the broker's sole control in administering a trust`)
       AND (NOT `the SEGC or Court is satisfied I contributed to the insolvency`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- reg 7.5.70(2): the claim "must be in writing and must be served on the SEGC: (a) if there has been published ... a
-- notice specifying a day on or before which claims may be made ... on or before that day; or (b) in any other case,
-- within 6 months after the person becomes aware of the dealer having become insolvent". (1): the notice day is "not
-- earlier than 3 months after the publication of the notice". (3): a late claim "is barred unless the SEGC otherwise
-- determines". Six months is read as ending on the same day of the sixth month after awareness.
@export By when must I serve my written claim on the SEGC for property my insolvent broker held (Corporations Regulations reg 7.5.70(2))?
GIVEN `the SEGC published a notice with a closing day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the SEGC published a notice (Form 720) naming a day on or before which claims about this broker may be made?
      `the closing day in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The closing day named in the notice (ISO date; any date if there is none)
      `the day I became aware of the insolvency` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware that the broker had become insolvent (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I make my NGF claim` IS
    IF `the SEGC published a notice with a closing day`
    THEN `the closing day in the notice`
    ELSE `the day N months after` `the day I became aware of the insolvency` 6

@export Is my claim on the National Guarantee Fund barred because it was late (Corporations Regulations reg 7.5.70(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the SEGC published a notice with a closing day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the SEGC published a notice naming a closing day for claims about this broker?
      `the closing day in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The closing day named in the notice (ISO date; any date if there is none)
      `the day I became aware of the insolvency` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware that the broker had become insolvent (ISO date)
      `the day I served my written claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you served your written claim on the SEGC (ISO date)
      `the SEGC determined otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the SEGC determined that a late claim is not barred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my NGF claim barred` IS
    IF `is on or before` `the day I served my written claim` (`By when must I make my NGF claim` `the SEGC published a notice with a closing day` `the closing day in the notice` `the day I became aware of the insolvency`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the SEGC determined otherwise`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `regs 7.5.72B(1), 7.5.78, 7.5.79 -- what the National Guarantee Fund can pay me`

-- reg 7.5.72B(1): the sum paid out of the Fund to one claimant for claims about one participant "referable to" one
-- event or circumstance "(c) must not exceed $1 million; and (d) to the extent that the eligible claims relate to cash
-- held with the participant ... immediately before the event or circumstance--must not exceed $250,000". The pro rata
-- cut in (3) (where all claims exceed the participant limit in reg 7.5.72A, 15% of the Fund's minimum amount) and any
-- SEGC determination under (4) are not encoded: the answer is the claimant limit before them.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `x` LESS THAN `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

@export What is the most the National Guarantee Fund may pay me for claims about one broker and one event, under the claimant limit (Corporations Regulations reg 7.5.72B(1))?
GIVEN `my allowed claims for cash held with the broker` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your allowed claims that relates to cash held with the broker immediately before the event, in dollars
      `my allowed claims for other property` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your allowed claims for securities and other property, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The most the NGF may pay me` IS
    `the smaller of` (`the smaller of` `my allowed claims for cash held with the broker` 250000 PLUS `my allowed claims for other property`) 1000000

-- reg 7.5.78: if the SEGC allows a claim in whole or part, or disallows it wholly only because the dealer compensated
-- the claimant before it was determined (and it would otherwise have been allowed), the claimant "is entitled to be
-- paid out of the Fund" the reasonable costs and disbursements of making and proving the claim, and of attempting to
-- recover the loss.
@export Am I entitled to be paid my reasonable costs of making my National Guarantee Fund claim (Corporations Regulations reg 7.5.78)?
GIVEN `the SEGC allowed my claim in whole or part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the SEGC allowed your claim, in whole or in part?
      `it was disallowed only because the broker compensated me first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the claim wholly disallowed because the broker compensated you before it was decided, when it would otherwise have been allowed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to my NGF claim costs` IS
    JUST (`the SEGC allowed my claim in whole or part` OR `it was disallowed only because the broker compensated me first`)

-- reg 7.5.79(1): interest "at the rate of 5% per annum or, if another rate is determined in writing by the SEGC, at that
-- other rate" on the amount payable (not counting costs and disbursements), for the period "beginning on the day on which
-- the person became entitled to make the claim and ending on" the day it is paid (in the ordinary case, (c)). (2)(b): a
-- determined rate "must not be less than 5% per year". Read here as simple interest on a 365-day year, counting the days
-- as the difference of the two dates.
@export How much interest must the National Guarantee Fund pay me on my compensation, paid in one sum (Corporations Regulations reg 7.5.79(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the compensation, not counting costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation payable to you, not counting costs and disbursements, in dollars
      `the day I became entitled to claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you became entitled to make the claim (ISO date)
      `the day it is paid` IS A DATE @desc The day the compensation is paid to you (ISO date)
      `the rate the SEGC determined` IS A NUMBER @desc A rate of interest the SEGC has determined in writing, as a fraction (e.g. 0.07 for 7%); 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The interest the NGF must pay me` IS
    (`the compensation, not counting costs` TIMES `the rate` TIMES `the days`) DIVIDED BY 365
    WHERE
        `the rate` MEANS
            IF `the rate the SEGC determined` AT LEAST 0.05
            THEN `the rate the SEGC determined`
            ELSE 0.05
        `the days` MEANS
            `the day number of` `the day it is paid` MINUS `the day number of` `the day I became entitled to claim`
